# Plan M7, step 4 (the author, 2026-11-10; the book, forms-declare-or-call): a structural form declares or calls and writes
# no known place.  `i: g()` with a known int place i is refused whatever its tail is -- here the result of a
# call.
fn: g () int
    return: 6
end: g
fn: f () int
    int: i 5
    i: g()
    return: i
end: f
send: exit(exit_code: f(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
